ent-CigaretteWH40KFootfallScene = clerk's cigarette
    .desc = A cigarette accompanying an unusually long administrative break.

wh40k-footfall-administration-administrationfinanceclerk-name = Administration accountant
wh40k-footfall-administration-administrationfinanceclerk-desc = A clerk reconciles terminal accounts and station expenses.
wh40k-footfall-administration-administrationfinanceclerk-marker = Spawn point: Administration accountant
ent-MobWH40KFootfallAdministrationFinanceClerk = { wh40k-footfall-administration-administrationfinanceclerk-name }
    .desc = { wh40k-footfall-administration-administrationfinanceclerk-desc }
ent-MarkerWH40KFootfallAdministrationFinanceClerk = { wh40k-footfall-administration-administrationfinanceclerk-marker }
    .desc = { wh40k-footfall-administration-marker-desc }
wh40k-footfall-administration-administrationfinanceclerk-line-1 = The monitor is red again. If I recolour the numbers green, is that improved reporting or heresy?
wh40k-footfall-administration-administrationfinanceclerk-line-2 = Our money never vanishes. It moves into 'unforeseen circumstances'. That column is growing faster than the station.
wh40k-footfall-administration-administrationfinanceclerk-line-3 = Someone booked the candles as emergency lighting. I am trying to work out why the emergency has lasted three quarters.
wh40k-footfall-administration-administrationfinanceclerk-line-4 = Payment processed does not mean order delivered. I keep those entries on separate screens for a reason.

wh40k-footfall-administration-administrationsmokingclerk-name = Smoking clerk
wh40k-footfall-administration-administrationsmokingclerk-desc = A clerk paces the office with a cigarette while postponing the reports.
wh40k-footfall-administration-administrationsmokingclerk-marker = Spawn point: Smoking clerk
ent-MobWH40KFootfallAdministrationSmokingClerk = { wh40k-footfall-administration-administrationsmokingclerk-name }
    .desc = { wh40k-footfall-administration-administrationsmokingclerk-desc }
ent-MarkerWH40KFootfallAdministrationSmokingClerk = { wh40k-footfall-administration-administrationsmokingclerk-marker }
    .desc = { wh40k-footfall-administration-marker-desc }
wh40k-footfall-administration-administrationsmokingclerk-line-1 = This is not a break. I am considering a document. It is a thick document, so the consideration involves smoke.
wh40k-footfall-administration-administrationsmokingclerk-line-2 = They issued an order banning smoking in the office. I am reviewing it. Until it is approved, the legal position is fascinating.
wh40k-footfall-administration-administrationsmokingclerk-line-3 = I walk to keep my thoughts moving. Paper cannot walk, unfortunately, so it stagnates on my behalf.
wh40k-footfall-administration-administrationsmokingclerk-line-4 = Maris asked when the report would be ready. I said after this cigarette. We did not record which cigarette.

wh40k-footfall-administration-administrationrecordsclerk-name = Administration registrar
wh40k-footfall-administration-administrationrecordsclerk-desc = A seated clerk checks applications and station records.
wh40k-footfall-administration-administrationrecordsclerk-marker = Spawn point: Administration registrar
ent-MobWH40KFootfallAdministrationRecordsClerk = { wh40k-footfall-administration-administrationrecordsclerk-name }
    .desc = { wh40k-footfall-administration-administrationrecordsclerk-desc }
ent-MarkerWH40KFootfallAdministrationRecordsClerk = { wh40k-footfall-administration-administrationrecordsclerk-marker }
    .desc = { wh40k-footfall-administration-marker-desc }
wh40k-footfall-administration-administrationrecordsclerk-line-1 = Your application says 'urgent'. We have a separate queue for that. It moves at the usual speed, but the name is encouraging.
wh40k-footfall-administration-administrationrecordsclerk-line-2 = Leave the third copy with me. Keep the second. Hold onto the first in case it turns out to be the correct one.
wh40k-footfall-administration-administrationrecordsclerk-line-3 = A misspelled name is easy to fix. A misspelled ship name has usually already departed.
wh40k-footfall-administration-administrationrecordsclerk-line-4 = I am not slowing the station down. I am preserving evidence that it worked at all.

wh40k-footfall-administration-administrationdispatchclerk-name = Administration dispatcher
wh40k-footfall-administration-administrationdispatchclerk-desc = A seated clerk coordinates maintenance, departmental requests and station work.
wh40k-footfall-administration-administrationdispatchclerk-marker = Spawn point: Administration dispatcher
ent-MobWH40KFootfallAdministrationDispatchClerk = { wh40k-footfall-administration-administrationdispatchclerk-name }
    .desc = { wh40k-footfall-administration-administrationdispatchclerk-desc }
ent-MarkerWH40KFootfallAdministrationDispatchClerk = { wh40k-footfall-administration-administrationdispatchclerk-marker }
    .desc = { wh40k-footfall-administration-marker-desc }
wh40k-footfall-administration-administrationdispatchclerk-line-1 = Cargo wants crate space, medicae want quiet, engineers want to be left alone. The meeting is going well: everyone has been bothered.
wh40k-footfall-administration-administrationdispatchclerk-line-2 = I scheduled the door repair for morning. Now it only admits people who know which side its morning is on.
wh40k-footfall-administration-administrationdispatchclerk-line-3 = Someone requested 'fix everything urgently'. I sent it back for clarification. 'Everything' belongs to several departments.
wh40k-footfall-administration-administrationdispatchclerk-line-4 = If someone says the station runs like clockwork, ask who winds the clock. Usually it is someone with a wrench and a very tired face.

wh40k-footfall-administration-publicresidentseatedone-name = Resident with receipts
wh40k-footfall-administration-publicresidentseatedone-desc = A seated resident sorts receipts and tries to understand the expenses.
wh40k-footfall-administration-publicresidentseatedone-marker = Spawn point: Resident with receipts
ent-MobWH40KFootfallPublicResidentSeatedOne = { wh40k-footfall-administration-publicresidentseatedone-name }
    .desc = { wh40k-footfall-administration-publicresidentseatedone-desc }
ent-MarkerWH40KFootfallPublicResidentSeatedOne = { wh40k-footfall-administration-publicresidentseatedone-marker }
    .desc = { wh40k-footfall-administration-marker-desc }
wh40k-footfall-administration-publicresidentseatedone-line-1 = I started recording every expense. Now I know exactly why I have no money. No practical benefit so far.
wh40k-footfall-administration-publicresidentseatedone-line-2 = Paid for lodging, paid for food. Now I need wages to arrive at the same pace.
wh40k-footfall-administration-publicresidentseatedone-line-3 = I am counting receipts. If the total is a pleasing number, I might at least respect the bill.
wh40k-footfall-administration-publicresidentseatedone-line-4 = On Footfall they say money should work. Mine seem to have found employment with someone else.

wh40k-footfall-administration-publicresidentseatedtwo-name = Resting resident
wh40k-footfall-administration-publicresidentseatedtwo-desc = A resident rests between shifts and talks about everyday station life.
wh40k-footfall-administration-publicresidentseatedtwo-marker = Spawn point: Resting resident
ent-MobWH40KFootfallPublicResidentSeatedTwo = { wh40k-footfall-administration-publicresidentseatedtwo-name }
    .desc = { wh40k-footfall-administration-publicresidentseatedtwo-desc }
ent-MarkerWH40KFootfallPublicResidentSeatedTwo = { wh40k-footfall-administration-publicresidentseatedtwo-marker }
    .desc = { wh40k-footfall-administration-marker-desc }
wh40k-footfall-administration-publicresidentseatedtwo-line-1 = I sat down for five minutes. By station time, this is still the best part of my shift.
wh40k-footfall-administration-publicresidentseatedtwo-line-2 = I like this chair. It does not ask where I am going, demand a pass or doubt where I belong.
wh40k-footfall-administration-publicresidentseatedtwo-line-3 = My neighbour snores like a cargo shuttle arriving. I might move nearer the actual docks; at least they have a schedule.
wh40k-footfall-administration-publicresidentseatedtwo-line-4 = If no alarm goes off today, I call it a holiday. We have few holidays, but we appreciate them.

wh40k-footfall-administration-publicresidentstandingone-name = Resident after a shift
wh40k-footfall-administration-publicresidentstandingone-desc = A resident talks about wages and station gossip after a shift.
wh40k-footfall-administration-publicresidentstandingone-marker = Spawn point: Resident after a shift
ent-MobWH40KFootfallPublicResidentStandingOne = { wh40k-footfall-administration-publicresidentstandingone-name }
    .desc = { wh40k-footfall-administration-publicresidentstandingone-desc }
ent-MarkerWH40KFootfallPublicResidentStandingOne = { wh40k-footfall-administration-publicresidentstandingone-marker }
    .desc = { wh40k-footfall-administration-marker-desc }
wh40k-footfall-administration-publicresidentstandingone-line-1 = Another crew promised to return rich. They returned. They prefer not to discuss the other half of the promise.
wh40k-footfall-administration-publicresidentstandingone-line-2 = The market seller said it was unique. Two stalls later I found three more unique items, all identical.
wh40k-footfall-administration-publicresidentstandingone-line-3 = Worked in the morning, tired in the evening. If tomorrow repeats, I can file a stability report.
wh40k-footfall-administration-publicresidentstandingone-line-4 = When a captain says 'short voyage', I look at their ration supply rather than their route.

wh40k-footfall-administration-publicresidentstandingtwo-name = Resident looking for a friend
wh40k-footfall-administration-publicresidentstandingtwo-desc = A resident waits for a friend and shares port news.
wh40k-footfall-administration-publicresidentstandingtwo-marker = Spawn point: Resident looking for a friend
ent-MobWH40KFootfallPublicResidentStandingTwo = { wh40k-footfall-administration-publicresidentstandingtwo-name }
    .desc = { wh40k-footfall-administration-publicresidentstandingtwo-desc }
ent-MarkerWH40KFootfallPublicResidentStandingTwo = { wh40k-footfall-administration-publicresidentstandingtwo-marker }
    .desc = { wh40k-footfall-administration-marker-desc }
wh40k-footfall-administration-publicresidentstandingtwo-line-1 = We agreed to meet 'by the door'. On a station with more doors than sensible decisions. Excellent planning.
wh40k-footfall-administration-publicresidentstandingtwo-line-2 = My friend went to buy a shuttle. I hope they at least walk back to collect me.
wh40k-footfall-administration-publicresidentstandingtwo-line-3 = I might join an expedition. First I want a profession where surviving earns a bonus instead of being expected.
wh40k-footfall-administration-publicresidentstandingtwo-line-4 = I get port news here. When things are quiet, we discuss the weather. Outside it is consistently lethal.

wh40k-footfall-administration-publicwindowwatcher-name = Void watcher
wh40k-footfall-administration-publicwindowwatcher-desc = A resident watches space through a window and thinks too long about the abyss.
wh40k-footfall-administration-publicwindowwatcher-marker = Spawn point: Void watcher
ent-MobWH40KFootfallPublicWindowWatcher = { wh40k-footfall-administration-publicwindowwatcher-name }
    .desc = { wh40k-footfall-administration-publicwindowwatcher-desc }
ent-MarkerWH40KFootfallPublicWindowWatcher = { wh40k-footfall-administration-publicwindowwatcher-marker }
    .desc = { wh40k-footfall-administration-marker-desc }
wh40k-footfall-administration-publicwindowwatcher-line-1 = The longer you stare into the abyss, the more it stares into you. I check the reflection occasionally, in case it is just the accountant behind me.
wh40k-footfall-administration-publicwindowwatcher-line-2 = The stars look motionless. I wish my life looked that way from outside, instead of like an unsecured crate.
wh40k-footfall-administration-publicwindowwatcher-line-3 = I am not waiting for a ship. Just listening to the silence. Glass and working atmospherics make it easier to bear.
wh40k-footfall-administration-publicwindowwatcher-line-4 = If something out there is watching us, I hope it cannot afford a ticket here either.

wh40k-footfall-administration-marker-desc = A saved source for one NPC. The arrow sets the original facing; seated actors need a real chair or bench.
wh40k-footfall-administration-maris-guide-port-choice = What is Footfall?
wh40k-footfall-administration-maris-guide-port-reply = Footfall is a port at the threshold of the Koronus Expanse. Travellers from Imperial space gather crews and supplies here before going farther. It grew around linked masses of stone, docks and habitable compartments. Metal, obligations and the habit of repairing things before they fall off keep us together.
wh40k-footfall-administration-maris-guide-authority-choice = Who runs this place?
wh40k-footfall-administration-maris-guide-authority-reply = Footfall has plenty of masters, merchant houses and people convinced their seal outranks everyone else's. My office handles station requests and our expedition administration. Engineers maintain the machinery, cargo handles supplies and the Arbites keep order. If an issue belongs elsewhere, I will direct you to whoever must answer for it. That is more useful than another ceremonial signature.
wh40k-footfall-administration-maris-guide-begin-choice = I have just arrived. Where should I begin?
wh40k-footfall-administration-maris-guide-begin-reply = First establish where you will sleep and eat. Medicae can treat wounds, the market supplies equipment and cargo handles orders. For vessels and routes, find Aveline Quill beside the shipyard consoles. Return to me for assignments: you will meet useful people and learn how this port works. Better to learn here than beyond a closed airlock.
wh40k-footfall-administration-maris-guide-law-choice = Which rules should I remember?
wh40k-footfall-administration-maris-guide-law-reply = Someone else's property does not become yours because it is poorly bolted down. Do not obstruct departments, enter restricted areas or settle debts with gunfire. Murochka Hawkins at the Arbites precinct can explain the law in detail. A Rogue Trader's warrant is a serious document. A spoken 'I am with the captain' is rather less serious.
wh40k-footfall-administration-maris-guide-work-choice = How do administrative assignments work?
wh40k-footfall-administration-maris-guide-work-reply = Ask me for work, read the assignment and accept it if you can meet its conditions. It stays in your quest log. Check whom to find, what to deliver and whom to report to: similar crates do not imply identical contents. Turn a completed assignment in to its issuer. I will listen to 'we tried very hard', but accounting has not learned to pay for that yet.
wh40k-footfall-administration-maris-guide-choice = Tell me about Footfall.
wh40k-footfall-administration-maris-guide-intro = Ask away. This is a large port, and a wrong turn can cost more than a good chart.
wh40k-footfall-administration-maris-guide-back = Return to other questions.

wh40k-footfall-administration-aveline-guide-purchase-choice = How do I buy a shuttle?
wh40k-footfall-administration-aveline-guide-purchase-reply = Use the shipyard console beside me. Remove your ID card from the PDA if necessary and insert it into the console slot. It must not already carry a deed to another vessel; ordinary purchases draw funds from your bank account. Choose an available vessel, check its price and purpose, then confirm. Retrieve the card afterwards: it now carries your ship's deed. You cannot register a second ship on the same occupied card.
wh40k-footfall-administration-aveline-guide-arrival-choice = I bought one. Where do I find it?
wh40k-footfall-administration-aveline-guide-arrival-reply = The yard delivers the vessel to the station. It docks if a compatible berth is available; otherwise it arrives nearby and needs a separate docking manoeuvre. Do not look for it inside this office or assume a particular airlock. Check the name on your deed and the navigation display, then locate it at the docks. If there is no safe passage, do not enter the void without a suit and air supply.
wh40k-footfall-administration-aveline-guide-deed-choice = Why should I protect the owner's card?
wh40k-footfall-administration-aveline-guide-deed-reply = The card carries the deed, and the ship's consoles are tied to that ownership. You need it for helm access and a shipyard sale. A friend's ordinary pass does not replace your deed. Arrange crew access and duties before undocking. A card left in the console can turn a captain into someone waving very persuasively beside their own ship.
wh40k-footfall-administration-aveline-guide-helm-choice = How do I leave the dock and fly?
wh40k-footfall-administration-aveline-guide-helm-reply = Find the shuttle console aboard and present the owner's card. Read the radar: locate the station, other vessels and obstacles. Check the departure lock; a newly purchased ship should not leave by itself. Once everyone is aboard and airlocks are closed, release the necessary locks, undock and move into clear space. Thrusters and turns require room. The neighbouring ship is not an expendable navigation aid.
wh40k-footfall-administration-aveline-guide-prepare-choice = What should I check before an expedition?
wh40k-footfall-administration-aveline-guide-prepare-reply = Check air, system power, hull integrity, repair supplies, medicine and suits. Mining needs tools and cargo space; a long voyage needs people who can use them. Check drive readiness and the return route, and count the crew before departure. Even the catalogue's most expensive ship cannot turn supplies left on the station into provisions aboard.
wh40k-footfall-administration-aveline-guide-sectors-choice = How does a sector route differ from radar?
wh40k-footfall-administration-aveline-guide-sectors-reply = Radar is for manoeuvring and docking within the current system. The sector chart shows systems and the routes linking them; a straight line drawn with your finger does not open a new passage. Select an available route at the ship's console and check drive readiness: system links and vessel restrictions apply. I can show you the current chart, but departure is controlled aboard. On a true warp voyage, a Navigator reads currents rather than admiring the gap between icons.
wh40k-footfall-administration-aveline-guide-uses-choice = What can I do with my own shuttle?
wh40k-footfall-administration-aveline-guide-uses-reply = Carry crews and supplies, mine, organise expeditions, explore accessible locations and bring cargo home. Capabilities depend on the vessel: hold size, equipment and crew matter more than a handsome name. Surface visits need a suitable arrival method and a way back; seeing a planet does not guarantee a convenient landing. Start with a voyage your equipment can support. Plan heroism after checking oxygen.
wh40k-footfall-administration-aveline-guide-sell-choice = How do I sell a shuttle?
wh40k-footfall-administration-aveline-guide-sell-reply = Return and dock at the station whose yard accepts the sale. Move valuables ashore and remove every living creature: the entire vessel, including cargo left aboard, will be scrapped. Insert the deed card into the shipyard console, check its valuation and confirm. Ordinary proceeds go to your bank account; valuation and yard terms determine the amount, not a promise of a full refund. Voucher-issued ships are handled separately and do not provide an ordinary cash payout.
wh40k-footfall-administration-aveline-guide-refusal-choice = Why does the console refuse?
wh40k-footfall-administration-aveline-guide-refusal-reply = For a purchase, check the inserted card, bank account, shipyard access and the vessel's availability in that yard's catalogue. A card already bound to a ship cannot register another. For a sale, check that the card belongs to that vessel, that it is docked at the correct station and that nobody remains aboard. Some objects also block a sale. Read the console's refusal message: it is terse, but usually more accurate than someone advising another twenty clicks.
wh40k-footfall-administration-aveline-guide-void-choice = What lies beyond Footfall?
wh40k-footfall-administration-aveline-guide-void-reply = The Koronus Expanse begins where the guidebook's confident voice becomes noticeably quieter. There are trade routes, forgotten holdings and places best approached by a prepared crew. The void does not distinguish pauper from captain: decompression makes the same convincing argument to both. Return by a known route, look after your ship and record where you have been. A fine story is worth more when its narrator comes back alive.
wh40k-footfall-administration-aveline-guide-chart = Show me the current sector chart.
wh40k-footfall-administration-aveline-guide-choice = Explain ship purchase and travel.
wh40k-footfall-administration-aveline-guide-intro = Let us cover the journey from the yard to your return. Which part do you need?
wh40k-footfall-administration-aveline-guide-back = Return to other questions.
